# Rclex — Clock, Time and Duration

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:rclex, github: "FelixPe/rclex"}
  ]
)
```

## About

`Rclex.Clock` wraps `rcl_clock_t`. Three clock types are supported:

* `:system_time` — wall clock; can jump.
* `:steady_time` — monotonic; never goes backwards.
* `:ros_time` — same as `:system_time` until you enable an override (e.g. for
  bag playback or simulation).

Reference implementations:

* C++ — [`rclcpp::Clock`](https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/blob/rolling/rclcpp/include/rclcpp/clock.hpp)
  and [`rclcpp::Time` / `rclcpp::Duration`](https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/blob/rolling/rclcpp/include/rclcpp/time.hpp)
* Python — [`rclpy.clock`](https://github.com/ros2/rclpy/blob/rolling/rclpy/rclpy/clock.py),
  [`rclpy.time`](https://github.com/ros2/rclpy/blob/rolling/rclpy/rclpy/time.py),
  [`rclpy.duration`](https://github.com/ros2/rclpy/blob/rolling/rclpy/rclpy/duration.py)
* Design — [Clock and Time in ROS 2](https://design.ros.org/articles/clock_and_time.html)

## A system clock

```elixir
:ok = Rclex.start_clock(clock_type: :system_time)

now = Rclex.now()
IO.puts("system now: #{Rclex.Time.to_seconds(now)} s")
IO.inspect(Rclex.Time.to_msg(now), label: "as builtin_interfaces/msg/Time")
```

## Time arithmetic

```elixir
alias Rclex.{Time, Duration}

t0 = Rclex.now()
Process.sleep(100)
t1 = Rclex.now()

dt = Time.sub(t1, t0)
IO.puts("elapsed: #{Duration.to_seconds(dt) * 1000} ms")

future = Time.add(t1, Duration.from_seconds(2.5))
IO.puts("2.5 s from now: #{Time.to_seconds(future)} s")
```

## A ROS-time clock with manual override

`:ros_time` clocks let you "drive" time manually — useful for replaying
recorded data or simulating without a real `/clock` publisher.

```elixir
:ok = Rclex.start_clock(name: :sim_clock, clock_type: :ros_time)

:ok = Rclex.Clock.enable(:sim_clock)

# Pretend it is exactly 1700000000 s since the epoch.
:ok = Rclex.Clock.set_ros_time_override(:sim_clock, 1_700_000_000_000_000_000)

t = Rclex.now(:sim_clock)
IO.puts("simulated now: #{Time.to_seconds(t)} s, clock_type: #{inspect(t.clock_type)}")
```

## Cleanup

```elixir
Rclex.stop_clock(:sim_clock)
Rclex.stop_clock()
```
